    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Question\n\n```nix\r\nflash.enable = true;\r\n```\r\nLet's say I have the above situation\r\nnow I want to change this to\r\n```nix\r\nflash = {\r\n  settings = something;\r\n  enable = true;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhen i try to add `{}` at `.` in between of `flash.enable` i expect enable to be pushed down a line.\r\n\r\ncurrently it stays like `flash{}enable` but i want it to go like\r\n```nix\r\nflash{}\r\nenable\r\n```\r\n\r\nthis behavior will make it easier",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pairs</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"flash.enable = true;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">flash</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\"><span class=\"pl-en\">enable</span></span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">true</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let's say I have the above situation<br>\nnow I want to change this to</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"flash = {\n  settings = something;\n  enable = true;\n};\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">flash</span></span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">settings</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">something</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">enable</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">true</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">when i try to add <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code> at <code class=\"notranslate\">.</code> in between of <code class=\"notranslate\">flash.enable</code> i expect enable to be pushed down a line.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">currently it stays like <code class=\"notranslate\">flash{}enable</code> but i want it to go like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"flash{}\nenable\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">flash</span></span><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">enable</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">this behavior will make it easier</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pairs\nQuestion\nflash.enable = true;\nLet's say I have the above situation\nnow I want to change this to\nflash = {\n  settings = something;\n  enable = true;\n};\nwhen i try to add {} at . in between of flash.enable i expect enable to be pushed down a line.\ncurrently it stays like flash{}enable but i want it to go like\nflash{}\nenable\nthis behavior will make it easier",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
