            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> currently it stays like `flash{}enable` but i want it to go like\r\n> \r\n> ```nix\r\n> flash{}\r\n> enable\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nSorry, but this behavior doesn't fit a design of 'mini.pairs' at all. The current behavior does, as it inserts a pair. For a more complex editing, use Normal mode actions/operators. For example, from 'mini.surround'.\r\n\r\nBut in this particular case I'd do something like this:\r\n- Put cursor on the `.` in Normal mode.\r\n- Press `x` to remove the dot.\r\n- Press `C` to remove all the text to the right (which puts `enable = true;` in the `\"` register) and starts Insert mode.\r\n- Press `{` to insert a `{}` pair.\r\n- Press `<CR>` to start new line from inside braces.\r\n- Press `<C-R>\"` to insert contents of `\"` register.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">currently it stays like <code class=\"notranslate\">flash{}enable</code> but i want it to go like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"flash{}\nenable\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">flash</span></span><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">enable</span></pre></div>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, but this behavior doesn't fit a design of 'mini.pairs' at all. The current behavior does, as it inserts a pair. For a more complex editing, use Normal mode actions/operators. For example, from 'mini.surround'.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But in this particular case I'd do something like this:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Put cursor on the <code class=\"notranslate\">.</code> in Normal mode.</li>\n<li>Press <code class=\"notranslate\">x</code> to remove the dot.</li>\n<li>Press <code class=\"notranslate\">C</code> to remove all the text to the right (which puts <code class=\"notranslate\">enable = true;</code> in the <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> register) and starts Insert mode.</li>\n<li>Press <code class=\"notranslate\">{</code> to insert a <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code> pair.</li>\n<li>Press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;CR&gt;</code> to start new line from inside braces.</li>\n<li>Press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-R&gt;\"</code> to insert contents of <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> register.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "currently it stays like flash{}enable but i want it to go like\nflash{}\nenable\n\nSorry, but this behavior doesn't fit a design of 'mini.pairs' at all. The current behavior does, as it inserts a pair. For a more complex editing, use Normal mode actions/operators. For example, from 'mini.surround'.\nBut in this particular case I'd do something like this:\n\nPut cursor on the . in Normal mode.\nPress x to remove the dot.\nPress C to remove all the text to the right (which puts enable = true; in the \" register) and starts Insert mode.\nPress { to insert a {} pair.\nPress <CR> to start new line from inside braces.\nPress <C-R>\" to insert contents of \" register.",
